agec is a simple file encryption tool that implements age format[1]
in C with minimal dependencies. The tool supports asymmetric
encryption based on X25519, and a passphrase encryption based on
scrypt.

For other implementations, tools, etc., see awesome-age list[2].

[1]: https://age-encryption.org
[2]: https://github.com/FiloSottile/awesome-age

Building and installing
-----------------------

On Unix-like systems the only library dependency apart from libc
is OpenSSL, which is used for portable random function. So to ditch
it you just need to edit unix/random.c file; that's straightforward
if you know the target system.

To build the utility run 'make' and to install run 'make install'.

On Plan 9 systems agec utilizes libc, libstdio and libsec; all of
them are available in the default install. To build and install
use mk(1). No apes are required.

Examples
--------

Encrypt and decrypt the secret with a passphrase:

    $ agec -p <secret.txt >secret.txt.age
    $ agec -d <secret.txt.age >secret.txt

Generate a password-protected key file, asymmetrically encrypt and
decrypt:

    $ agecgen | agec -p >key
    Public key: age19a79get8k27m20w6j3z7jw5xarn22u2lhf6rpwg2hqpg83vk
    msus3k4m7f
    Enter passphrase:
    $ agec \
      -r age19a79get8k27m20w6j3z7jw5xarn22u2lhf6rpwg2hqpg83vkmsus3k4m7f \
      <secret.txt >secret.txt.age
    $ agec -d -ikey secret.txt.age >secret.txt

Print the encrypted secret on paper, wrapping it in ASCII armor:

    $ agec -ap <secret.txt | lpr

For more info see manual pages in doc/ directory.

Compatibility
-------------

agec aims to be compliant with v1 specification[3] (also available
at doc/age.5). The tool passes all test vectors[4] except for some
in test/vectors/dec-wontfix directory.

The tool diverges from these cases being stricter about decoding
ASCII armored input: it accepts only LF as a line ending, disallows
whitespace before and after the PEM block and enforces LF at the end
of the last line.

These cases seems not to be directly required by the specification.

To do a test, run 'make check-vectors'. It doesn't include
dec-wontfix vectors.

The keyfile format is compatible with the reference implementation[5].
The invocation format is somewhat similar but is not compatible.

[3]: https://age-encryption.org/v1
[4]: https://age-encryption.org/testkit
[5]: https://github.com/FiloSottile/age

